Names are generated call signs; map tiles are typed classes and maps load from files the server ships to clients.                                                                                                                                                                              
Three web-client lessons: a piped build hid a syntax error and shipped 3 stale bundles; Defold resumes audio only from a canvas pointer; and a Lua buffer-stream write is one C call per float, so vwbuf writes whole shapes and CPU fell 40%->12%. Bombs splash on hits, not timeouts.        
No start screen: you land flying, escape opens a menu tree over the live arena, hull change is a respawn and works in zones. single_file.py injects viewport meta and draws its own starfield while wasm compiles. Weapons are one table model: bounce, proximity, splinter, push.             
Zones own their rules: settings ship over the wire, weapons are named in the zone file, apply_config rebuilds from baseline so reload is idempotent. Tech tree: levels are ladder rungs, add-ons are fire-time transforms per trigger, and greens are untyped until picked up.                 
Prize weights are relative, read against the hull's pool; rust corrodes only what a pilot holds. Charges are a pattern plus an inventory, ready slot in button bits. Bounty is derived from what you hold; points are the victim's bounty, so a fresh spawn is worth nothing.                  
Bots hunt by bounty/distance and chase greens. Tuning comes from ASSS dist/conf/svs, not invention: rounds inherit ship velocity so slower-than-ships is deliberate; multifire +50% energy +100% cooldown per rung; weights 40 stat/25 level/30 multi/70 charge.                               
The original gates almost nothing per ship (charges, multifire, bounce, prox, shrapnel all universal; its per-ship diff is nine settings). spawn_prizes=30 loads every spawn and flattens bot skill, so calibration pins it to 0. The arena is the full 1024-tile map.                         
Silent failures: a short Rust mirror is heap corruption (sim_sizeof_* guards it), an overflowing vec layer drops primitives. Perf: snapshots halved (prize tile coords + interest radius), sim_step lost a third; load time is the host's brotli already.                                      
Mobile HUD reworked: energy and bounty on your own hull, scoreboard behind a default-off 'info' toggle, flags as pennants, and one bottom row of controls -- a drawn d-pad left, then guns, bombs and a tappable pad per charge right.                                                         
Touch flight: the stick asks for a course, not a facing; a thumb arcs, so sweeps hold the rudder until it lands, timed in seconds. Zone model redesigned (decisions 23-26): one arena per process, directories relay only own observations, arenas pick their type.                            
Duels removed for now (decision 16 deferred, design kept): C2S_DUEL, the Duel mode, its Lua copy and Zone's arena map out, sim_map_duel is sim_map_pit. Web build needs bob from GitHub releases and JDK 25. Debug builds always panicked at startup on a u16 overflow at the 9th bot.         
Web build needs bob.jar from GitHub releases and JDK 25 at /opt/jdk25. A debug build could never start a zone: (i as u16)*8192 overflowed at the 9th bot. ASSS per-ship diff is 10 capability flags of 84. A room is 79 KB at 1.6-16 us/tick, so hosting cost is egress, not compute.          
Hosting is Vultr (own IPs, so Docker host-networking and UDP work; Fly rejected as HTTP-only). ASSS never capped an arena, so our SIM_MAX_SHIPS=64 is stricter than the original and cheap to raise. Repel is hostile only now, firer included.                                                
Fleet design is documented and its questions closed (no chat, DNS directories, per-zone max_ships and max_rooms). Bots never fired a bomb: both or-ed BTN_BOMB onto a held BTN_FIRE, and a held gun wins; they release it now, and only when the bomb out-rates it.                            
The roster now runs the original's numbers exactly: identical flight on all eight hulls, bomb levels buying blast not damage, prox widening a tile a level, scattered shrapnel. Every one of those settings is a zone.toml key rather than a constant.                                         
Weapons and flight match ASSS exactly; MultiFireAngle, BounceFactor and the prize economy do not. Hulls are identical without greens, so all spread is the tech tree: freeze +0.15 K/D, multifire neutral. Bots still never bomb. And the client has a generated synthwave loop.               
Deployment happened and hardened: ufw and blind-channel lessons from deploying with no shell, then the game live on one Vultr box behind Caddy with a security pass over inputs, capabilities, metadata and DNS.                                                                               
